docs: register the skill with CodeBuddy and document the process

Adds install/codebuddy.md and wires CodeBuddy into the READMEs, which
previously covered only Claude Code, Copilot and Cursor.

install/codebuddy.md
- Documents the two discovery locations: user scope ~/.codebuddy/skills/ and
  project scope <project>/.codebuddy/skills/
- Gives the PowerShell sync commands for Windows, where the bash examples are
  awkward
- Records why a directory junction is the wrong tool here: Node reports a
  junction as isSymbolicLink=true and isDirectory=false, so a loader that
  filters entries with isDirectory() never sees it. Verified against the
  installed skills directory before writing this down.
- Documents verification: the expected layout, and how settings.json
  disabledSkillsByPath can silently disable a skill

README.md / README.en.md
- CodeBuddy added to Quick Start, the per-platform install list and the
  supported-host list
- Corrected the English project tree, which still claimed README.md was the
  English file and that assets/ held localized READMEs (both stale since the
  Chinese-primary switch)

Registered locally at ~/.codebuddy/skills/general-readme-skill as a real
directory (not a junction) containing SKILL.md, references/, install/,
examples/, assets/, README.md, README.en.md and LICENSE. Dev-only material
(.git, benchmark_readmes/, benchmark_analysis.md) is deliberately excluded.
Validator passes; the skill is not present in disabledSkillsByPath.
